## Origin

2026-09-27 - operator hard rule in two steps. First, agreement to remove WA
branding universally. Then, on seeing a sweep in progress, the instruction
to use terminology found in CMMC and other regulatory frameworks because WA
is not an industry term. The term was verified against the published CMMC
Level 2 practices CM.L2-3.4.1 and CM.L2-3.4.2 and the NIST SP 800-53
configuration-management family rather than chosen from market usage;
"endpoint posture", picked earlier in the same session as market
vocabulary, was rejected for appearing in no framework.
